WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:09.170
Hi I'm Mine Cetinkaya-Rundel. I'm a
professor at Duke University

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:11.480
and a developer educator at Posit.

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:14.150
This year at posit:conf I'm
teaching a one-day teaching

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:15.740
data science master class.

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:18.740
I've been teaching data science
with R for over a decade.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:20.300
And I can't wait
to share everything

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:23.210
I've learned over this time
about successful data science

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:25.910
pedagogy, teaching
with authentic tools,

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:28.460
and doing so effectively
and efficiently.

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.200
Here are the top
three reasons why

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.270
you should take this workshop.

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:35.990
First reason is keeping up
with the evolving data science

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:37.670
ecosystem is not trivial.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:40.730
Keeping up with it and deciding
whether it's the right time

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:42.590
to update your
curriculum to incorporate

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:45.890
new tools or new features
of existing tools, new data

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:48.440
sources or new
workflows, and doing

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:51.350
so while concurrently
teaching can be overwhelming.

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:53.180
This workshop is
designed to share

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:55.340
with you what's new in
the land of teaching data

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:57.920
science with R and
to distill for you how

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:00.890
you can implement these
updates in your curricula.

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:03.050
Second, successful
teaching doesn't

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:05.150
end with successful
curriculum design.

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:08.030
The computational infrastructure
you use for your teaching

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:11.030
is an equally important part
of a successful data science

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:13.940
course, particularly if
your definition of success

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.400
takes into consideration
the experience

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:19.477
and enjoyment of your students
as well as of yourself.

00:01:19.477 --> 00:01:21.560
In this workshop, we'll
tell quite a bit about how

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:24.740
to set up computational teaching
environments with Posit Cloud

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:26.810
as well as other
server-based tools.

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:30.290
How to use Git and GitHub for
version control collaboration

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:32.390
and as your course
management system

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:34.940
and how to teach reproducible
authoring with Quarto

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:37.080
as well as how to use
it to build your course

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:39.000
materials and sites.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.150
And third, this workshop will
supercharge your learning

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:43.290
and teaching prep.

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:45.450
In one day of the
workshop, you will pick up

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:47.520
a wealth of information
and tips that

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:50.940
can save you weeks and months
of trial and error on your own.

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:53.910
Additionally, you'll meet a
community of like-minded data

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:55.920
science educators
with whom you can stay

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:57.960
in touch beyond the conference.

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:01.230
One final comment is that this
year, the teaching data science

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:04.050
workshop is offered as a
one-day workshop, which

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:05.970
means you can focus
on your teaching

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:09.060
on one of the workshop days and
spend the other day learning

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:11.940
something you've been hoping
to make time for all year.

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:15.640
Go to posit.co/conference to
register for this workshop,

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:18.480
as well as to find out about
all of the other fantastic

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:21.510
workshops we're offering
at posit::conf this year.

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:25.250
Looking forward to seeing
you in Chicago in September.

